<poml>
  <meta>
    <id>meta.plan.poml-go-sdk</id>
    <version>0.1.0</version>
    <owner>poml-go-sdk</owner>
  </meta>
  <role>Reference-quality test and badge roadmap, prioritizing underused test styles with the highest signal for CI badges.</role>

  <task>Badge targets mapped to new tests (prioritized by usefulness × rarity)</task>
  <cp caption="Badge + test backlog">
    <list>
      <item>Coverage/Codecov (High, fuzz): Add property-based fuzz cases for ParseString/ParseStringFast → Encode/Validate round-trips; seed corpus from poml/testdata and malformed samples to raise coverage and find panics.</item>
      <item>Deterministic outputs (High, golden): Golden snapshots for convertMarkdownToPOML/convertOrgToPOML and DeckGL/Graphviz renderers to enable a “Golden tests” badge and stabilize changes.</item>
      <item>Path safety (High, boundary): Image/media path escape tests (symlink + ..), size-limit enforcement for readFileWithLimit/media bodies; feeds security/govulncheck documentation badge.</item>
      <item>Integration/E2E matrix (High, integration): Expand semantic_test.go to include BaseDir + MaxMediaBytes options; add an extra OS/arch runner (arm64) badge and “Matrix E2E” badge.</item>
      <item>Fast/strict parser fidelity (Medium, differential): Tests comparing default vs fast vs strict options on whitespace preservation and validation failures; supports “Parser fidelity” badge.</item>
      <item>Concurrency safety (Medium, race/unit): Tests for ConverterRegistry concurrent Register/List to justify a “Thread-safe registry” badge.</item>
      <item>Builder completeness (Medium, combinatorial): Table-driven tests covering remaining builder methods (OutputFormat, Style, Raw, System/Human/Assistant ordering) to improve coverage badge resilience.</item>
      <item>Limits/DoS hardening (Medium, limit): Tests for base64 size limits and negative/zero limit semantics to back a “Resource limits enforced” badge.</item>
      <item>Docs pipeline (Medium, docs): MDX render smoke test (npx mdx README.mdx) to align with a “Docs build” badge.</item>
      <item>Lint/vuln badges (Low, monitoring): Keep golangci-lint/govulncheck jobs and badges; add go vet job with a badge (no new tests, but ensure it runs).</item>
    </list>
  </cp>

  <task>Execution order for “15 green badges”</task>
  <cp caption="Sequenced steps">
    <list>
      <item>1) Implement fuzz + boundary tests (coverage/security badges), wire Codecov badge.</item>
      <item>2) Add golden render/converter tests (golden badge) and parser fast/strict differentials.</item>
      <item>3) Extend semantic E2E for limits/BaseDir; add arm64 runner; publish matrix/E2E badge.</item>
      <item>4) Concurrency tests for registry and builder completeness tables; add go vet job/badge.</item>
      <item>5) Add docs smoke test; publish docs badge; ensure release/semantic-release badge present.</item>
    </list>
  </cp>

  <output-format>Keep this file concise; update as badges land.</output-format>
</poml>
